      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not provide an explicit definitional basis for “Intergroup conflict is conflict between social groups”; it discusses a study about perceptions (rival vs enemy) and conflict escalation, but does not define the term in those terms.",
        "The claim that intergroup conflict “can become tied to collective identity” is only indirectly supported by the study’s measure “conflict-related identity relevance,” not as a general definitional statement about intergroup conflict.",
